-- Scene 2: a CLOSED enumeration becomes a closed alternation --
  [OK] the choices become an alternation, and only those choices

-- Scene 3: optional fields and lists keep their arity --
  [OK] an optional field is optional in the root
  [OK] an optional list may be empty (zero or more)
  [OK] a REQUIRED list must hold at least one element (one or more)
  [OK] every emitted line is a whole rule -- no terminal carries a raw newline

-- Scene 4: what the grammar CANNOT carry, said out loud --
  [OK] the dropped constraints are reported
  [OK] ...by field
  [OK] ...and by operator
  [OK] ...saying WHY a grammar cannot carry them
  [OK] ...and that the court still does
  [OK] a schema with no :must constraints reports NOTHING unenforced
  [OK] the COURT still refuses what the grammar could not express

-- Scene 5: what cannot be expressed is REFUSED, never flattened --
  [OK] a nested structure is not expressible as a flat grammar
  [OK] ...so ToGBNF() refuses rather than emitting something else
  [OK] ...with a NAMED code
  [OK] ...naming the field
  [OK] ...and saying what the refusal protects
  [OK] the same schema is still perfectly valid for the COURT, which is the point

